  "notes": "CONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- Negative: なぞらえない\n- Te-form: なぞらえて\n- Past: なぞらえた\n\nUSAGE:\nThe pattern is AをBになぞらえる (to liken A to B). Often used in literary, analytical, or artistic contexts.\n\nWRITING:\nSometimes written as {準|なぞら}える or {擬|なぞら}える, but hiragana is most common.\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal and literary. More common in written language and speeches than in casual conversation.",
